From: Thorch contributors
Subject: [PATCH] input: qcom-hv-haptics: fix missing rc in hpwr_vreg error logs

Two haptics_enable_hpwr_vreg() failure sites log a %d conversion with no
argument to match it. sweep_run_store() is one:

	rc = haptics_enable_hpwr_vreg(chip, false);
	if (rc < 0)
		dev_err(chip->dev, "disable hpwr_vreg failed\n");

gcc reports -Wformat= here, and with no argument the conversion reads an
uninitialised register on the variadic path, so the message prints
garbage. This one sits on the manual sweep path, which is the sweep used
to exercise the actuator on the Thor, so a rail failure during a sweep
logged nothing usable.

haptics_stop_constant_effect_play() has the same defect one function
above, on the log this patch series leans on hardest: that work runs
after every bounded play, so a rail failure there logged a bare message
with a garbage number. Fix it in the same commit, since both are the same
one-token mistake and a sweep failure and a per-play stop failure are the
same class of event to whoever reads the log.

The other haptics_enable_hpwr_vreg() failure sites in this driver all
pass rc. These two were missed. Pass rc at both, matching the siblings.
---
 drivers/input/misc/qcom-hv-haptics.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/input/misc/qcom-hv-haptics.c
+++ b/drivers/input/misc/qcom-hv-haptics.c
@@ -2698,7 +2698,7 @@
 
 	rc = haptics_enable_hpwr_vreg(chip, false);
 	if (rc < 0)
-		dev_err(chip->dev, "disable hpwr_vreg failed\n");
+		dev_err(chip->dev, "disable hpwr_vreg failed, rc=%d\n", rc);
 }
 
 static int haptics_upload_effect(struct input_dev *dev,
@@ -5838,7 +5838,7 @@
 
 	rc = haptics_enable_hpwr_vreg(chip, false);
 	if (rc < 0)
-		dev_err(chip->dev, "disable hpwr_vreg failed, rc=%d\n");
+		dev_err(chip->dev, "disable hpwr_vreg failed, rc=%d\n", rc);
 
 	return count;
 }
